%N A402227 Triangle read by rows: T(n,k) is the number of labeled Hamiltonian digraphs with n vertices and k arcs, without loops, n >= 2, 0 <= k <= n*(n-1).
%H A402227 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A402227/b402227.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..74</a>
%F A402227 Let C_n be the set of directed Hamiltonian cycles on {1,...,n}. For each nonempty subset S of C_n, let E(S) be the union of the arc sets of the cycles in S. Then
%F A402227 Sum_{k=0..n*(n-1)} T(n,k)*x^k = Sum_{S subseteq C_n, S != {}} (-1)^(|S|+1) * x^|E(S)| * (1+x)^(n*(n-1)-|E(S)|).
%F A402227 Also, Sum_{k=0..n*(n-1)} T(n,k) = A326219(n).
%e A402227 Triangle begins:
